The point is that you have to pay attention to AC. I wouldn't go near a
minotaur, or anywhere I might run into a minotaur, unless I had enough
armor/protection. Spending adequate time and effort to advance your AC
is part of a good nethack strategy. Maybe I'm too snobbish, but in
general, if you ever feel like you *need* to genocide something, that
means you haven't been preparing your character adequately to face the
dangers of the dungeon (or haven't learnt to deal effectively with
certain types of monsters). This is especially true of melee monsters.


